===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|handen}}, {{m|enm|honden}}, from the noun (see above); and also from {{m|enm|henden}} (> {{cog|en|hend}}), from {{inh|en|ang|*hendan}}, {{m|ang|ġehendan|t=to seize by hand, grasp, hold}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*handijan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*handijaną|t=to take by hand, grasp}}, from the noun (see above). Cognate with {{cog|ofs|handa}}, {{m|ofs|henda|t=to grasp, seize}}, {{cog|gml|handen}}, {{m|gml|henden}} (in derivatives), {{cog|nl|handen}}, {{m|nl|henden|t=to arrange, dispose, be handy}}, {{cog|nl|overhandigen|t=to hand, hand over}}, {{cog|gmh|handen|t=to cut, hew}}, {{cog|gmh|henden|t=to give hands to; take hold of, seize}}, {{cog|non|henda|t=to grasp, seize, take by hand}}.

