#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 March 8|author=Paul Salveson|title=Fond farewells to two final trains...|journal=RAIL|issue=978|page=54|text=However, Anyon Kay remembers a Mr Walton Ainsworth, of Beech House, Rivington, who owned mills in Bolton, being a regular user before the First World War. He used to drive by horse and trap from his mansion to catch the 0906 train to Bolton each day. Before arriving at the station, local newsagent Tom Dutton would '''hand''' Mr Ainsworth his morning paper!}}
